---
id: org.dxos.ui.react-ui-feed
name: FeedSpec
version: 0.1.0
---

Consolidation spec for the feed spike. The spike answered "can one anchor-placed window scroll
smoothly with a CodeMirror editor per row" (yes — `DESIGN.md` has the principles, `TESTING.md` the
manual evidence). This document specifies the four parts to consolidate — **virtualizer**, **list**,
**outliner**, **minimap** — the seams between them, and what is an aspect (a policy the host may
swap, exposed as a reusable hook per the `react-ui-list` pattern) versus an internal (an invariant
the engine must hold, never exposed).

Status 2026-08-18: **implemented** — the virtualizer and debug entry points exist, the model and
the five aspects are in, the rails moved, and the flagship `assistant/Assistant` story exercises
the whole loop. Additions found by building: `ListModel.patch` (streaming for frozen items — an
identity-preserving replacement announced as `updated`), and the follow's speeds raised for
streaming (8 rows/s; the class defaults were tuned for a single arrival).

Decisions taken:

- The virtualizer shipped as an entry point of this package first, then graduated to
  `@dxos/react-ui-virtual` (placement, `useWindow`/`Window`, the follow, and `ListModel`);
  this package depends on it and keeps the message-native layer.
- The list consumes a **model**, not an array: a low-level `ListModel` (reactive via `@effect/atom`)
  the virtualizer binds to, and `FeedModel` as the native case — not an add-on. `fromMessages()`
  keeps the array form as an adapter.
- The follow glide (`ScrollFollower`) is wired and on by default; instant is the fallback.
- Search is **not** the list's concern. Cross-cutting per-item data — search highlights, selection —
  reaches items through provider + hook (the decoration pattern, §Aspects); the list neither knows
  nor routes it.
- The rails live in **this package**: `Minimap` is promoted here, and `Outline` moves here from
  `react-ui-components` — call sites updated, no compatibility re-export.
- The horizontal axis is in scope for the **virtualizer** (axis-neutral arithmetic, an inline
  acceptance story against real content) and out of scope for the **feed list** (vertical only;
  rails stay vertical until a horizontal consumer exists).

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`   |
| `aspect`    | `org.dxos.mdl.aspect@0.1`      |

## Types

```mdl
type Extents
  desc: >
    The host's answer about row sizes, in scalars along one axis — never height or width, so the
    axis stays the DOM binding's business. `exact` means never revised by measurement (deterministic
    layouts: fixed-height rows, declared-width cards) but still checked in dev via onMismatch.
  fields:
    of: (index: number) => number
    exact?: boolean
```

```mdl
type Layout
  desc: The mounted range and where its parent goes. Everything a DOM binding needs, per commit.
  fields:
    first: number                     # first mounted row (visible + overscan)
    last: number
    visible: { first, last }          # what the reader can actually see — readouts describe this
    offset: number                    # absolute position of the first mounted row
    sizerExtent: number               # total scrollable extent, reserve included
```

```mdl
type WindowState
  desc: >
    Published state for chrome that lives outside the scroller — toolbar, statusbar, rails.
    Geometry is in pixels (what a map draws); indices are model-space (what a readout names).
  fields:
    index: number                     # row at the top of the viewport
    visible: { first, last }
    mounted: { first, last }
    count: number
    geometry: { scroll, viewport, total, window: { start, extent } }
```

```mdl
type ListModel
  desc: >
    The low-level contract the virtualizer binds to — what the engine already consumed as separate
    props (count, getId, extents), made one reactive object. Backed by @effect/atom, so derivations
    (stops, decorations, readouts) are atoms over it rather than parallel props. Changes carry
    structure the engine currently has to infer: a prepend says it is one, so anchor preservation
    is information, not an identity scan.
  fields:
    count: Atom<number>
    getId: (index: number) => string
    at: (index: number) => T | undefined
    changes: Stream<{ prepended?: number, appended?: number, updated?: string[] }>
```

```mdl
type FeedModel
  desc: >
    The native case, not an add-on: a ListModel of messages with the feed's own semantics. Owns
    ITERATION — how the window walks the source — so reaching an edge asks the model
    (loadBefore/loadAfter: paged history, reverse-from-tail) instead of leaking a host callback.
    Owns the stops policy and the streaming tail. Adapters: fromMessages(array) for the plain case;
    ECHO/queue bindings live outside this package (plugin-assistant adapts).
  extends: ListModel
  fields:
    stops: Atom<Stop[]>               # pluggable policy: per message | prompt | block | day
    streamingId?: Atom<string>        # tail message reconciling by delta
    loadBefore?: () => Promise<void>  # consumed by onEdge('start') — paging is the model's business
    loadAfter?: () => Promise<void>
```

```mdl
type Decoration
  desc: >
    A range of one item's rendered text that some producer wants painted — search is ONE producer;
    linting, mentions, and diff spans are others. Keyed by item id; delivered to items via the
    decoration provider/hook (§Aspects), never through list props.
  fields:
    id: string                        # item (message) id
    range: { offset: number, length: number }
    kind: string                      # producer tag: 'search' | 'mention' | ...
```

```mdl
type Stop
  desc: >
    One position navigation can land on. Stops are produced by a pluggable policy over the model
    (per message, per prompt, per block, per search hit, per day divider) and consumed identically
    by every driver: toolbar, arrow keys, outliner, minimap.
  fields:
    index: number                     # row the stop lives in
    id: string                        # model identity, survives reordering
    label?: string                    # what a rail or readout shows for it
```

```mdl
type Marker
  desc: An outliner tick's model. Range is in the host's own position space.
  fields:
    id: string
    title: string
    description?: string
    range: { from: number, to: number }
```

```mdl
type EdgeDrift
  desc: What reaching an edge revealed about the estimates. Reported, never silently applied.
  fields:
    edge: 'start' | 'end'
    delta: number
```

## Components

```mdl
component Virtualizer
  desc: >
    The reusable placement engine: Placement (pure arithmetic, no DOM/React) + useWindow (binding
    to an element the HOST owns) + Window (the trivial own-scroller binding for stories and simple
    hosts). Target: extractable package or react-ui-list aspect; retrofit candidate for
    react-ui-mosaic VirtualStack, which still runs tanstack react-virtual.
  props:
    model: ListModel                  # count + identity + change structure; array via fromMessages()
    extents: Extents                  # measurements stay keyed by model id, never by index
    axis?: 'block' | 'inline'         # default block; only the binding maps extent to height/width
    overscan?: number                 # rows mounted before/beyond the visible window, per side (8)
    reserve?: number                  # empty extent after the last row, part of the resting view
    sticky?: boolean                  # follow the tail as content arrives
  state:
    anchor: { id, index, start }      # the one authoritative position; everything else derived
    measured: Map<id, extent>
  actions:
    scrollToIndex(index, align?, behavior?)   # smooth only across mounted rows; far targets jump
  emits:
    onChange(state: WindowState)
    onEdge(drift: EdgeDrift)
    onMismatch({ index, id, declared, actual })   # exact means do-not-correct, not do-not-check
  layout: |
    scroller (host's; overflow-anchor: none — exactly one party anchors)
    ├── sizer      (extent only, holds no rows; what the thumb measures)
    └── window     (one absolutely positioned parent, moved by transform)
        └── rows   (unpositioned, in flow — the browser reflows followers)
```

```mdl
component MessageList
  desc: >
    The chat feed built on the Virtualizer. Composite: Root (headless — model mapping, aspects,
    context) / Viewport (ScrollArea binding of useWindow) / Item (one message, renderable outside
    the window too). Renders no toolbar or statusbar; useMessageList() exposes state and controls
    for chrome outside the scroller.
  props:
    model: FeedModel                            # or fromMessages(array); stops/streaming/paging live here
    renderer?: (message) => ItemContent         # resolves each message to a block kind
    Chrome?: Component<MessageChromeProps>      # host render-prop; avatar/timestamp/fork controls
    Custom?: Component                          # renderer for kind 'custom'
    registry?: XmlWidgetRegistry                # XML tag -> React widget
    estimateSize?: number | (message, index) => number
    stickyBottom?: boolean
    tailLines?: number                          # blank lines below the tail at rest; 0 by default
    overscan?: number
    debug?: boolean                             # borders, outlines + jump detector
    # NOT here, deliberately: decorations (née hits) and selection reach items via provider + hook
    # (§Aspects); isAnchor/streamingId are model concerns (FeedModel.stops / .streamingId).
  state:
    currentIndex: number                        # row containing the scroll offset — derived, never set beside it
    widgetStore: WidgetStateStore               # outlives rows; widget state survives unmount/remount
  actions:
    stepAnchor(delta)                           # one seam for every driver: toolbar, arrows, rails
    scrollToIndex(index, options?)
    scrollToBottom(options?)
```

```mdl
component Outline
  desc: >
    Index-space rail: one tick per stop, thinned to a fixed pitch, each tick standing for the span
    to the next. One popover card tracks the shown tick's center via a separate zero-height anchor —
    ticks are never wrapped, element identity must stay stable. MOVES here from react-ui-components
    (call sites updated, no re-export).
  props:
    markers: Marker[]
    visibleRange?: { from, to }       # markers intersecting it render active
    tickSize?: number                 # 8px; fixed pitch, rail thins to what fits
    width?: number                    # 32px (2rem), matches Minimap
  state:
    pointer: number | null            # tick under the pointer
    navigated: number | null          # tick the keyboard has navigated to
    shown: number | null              # which of the two wins; published as data-shown
  actions:
    onSelect(marker, index)
    onNavigate(delta)                 # to be replaced by the shared navigation aspect
  emits:
    data-pointer, data-navigated, data-shown   # observable invariants (DESIGN §12)
```

```mdl
component Minimap
  desc: >
    Content-space rail: the document in miniature, drawn from WindowState.geometry only. Track =
    total extent (reserve included); faint band = mounted window; solid band = viewport. Promoted
    from testing/debug to a sibling of Outline in this package. Debug overlays (per-row extents, drift) stay in
    testing/debug.
  props:
    state: WindowState
    width?: number                    # 32px (2rem), asserted equal to Outline's
  actions:
    onSelect(fraction)                # host maps fraction to offset via the navigation seam
```

## Aspects

The `react-ui-list` pattern: standalone, tested hooks that components compose. The dividing rule —
**a policy the host may swap is an aspect; an invariant the engine must hold is an internal.**
Internals (the anchor, prepend detection, the id-keyed measurement pass, the single writer of the
scroll) are never exposed: a hook over an invariant invites a second party into exactly the seams
the design keeps single-owner.

```mdl
aspect useWindow
  desc: The virtualizer itself, bound to a scroller the host owns. Already exists.
  owns: placement, layout, sticky intent, measurement pass
```

```mdl
aspect useStops
  desc: >
    Navigation stops as an atom over the model (FeedModel.stops): per message, per prompt (user
    turns), per block, per day divider. Shared by list, outliner, minimap so a per-prompt feed
    shows per-prompt ticks with no extra wiring. isAnchor survives as fromMessages() sugar for the
    per-message policy.
  owns: stops policy over ListModel
```

```mdl
aspect useDecorations
  desc: >
    THE PATTERN for cross-cutting per-item data, retrofitted everywhere rather than invented per
    surface: a provider at the host carries producers (search, mentions, lint, diff); an item asks
    useDecorations(id) for its own ranges and paints them. The list neither knows nor routes —
    search leaves the list API entirely (searchFeed stays a model-level producer, since
    virtualization hides most items from any DOM search). Candidate consumers beyond the feed:
    react-ui-editor documents, tables, grid cells.
  owns: provider of Decoration producers; per-item subscription by id
```

```mdl
aspect useItemSelection
  desc: >
    The item-side hook of the same pattern: an item asks for its own { selected, toggle, rowProps }
    by id instead of the list threading selectedIds through props. Backed by useListSelection's
    modes (single | multi | range) at the provider; model-space ids, so virtualization is untouched.
  owns: per-item selection binding by id
```

```mdl
aspect useFeedNavigation
  desc: >
    Step/jump intents over a WindowController plus stops — the ONE seam every driver calls
    (toolbar buttons, arrow keys, outliner, minimap). Cursor derives from the scroll offset, so
    every press travels. Smooth-vs-jump policy lives here, not in each caller: smooth within the
    mounted window, instant beyond it. Distinct from react-ui-list useListNavigation, which is
    focus traversal over fully-mounted rows — different problem, same naming family.
  owns: step(delta), jumpTo(stop), currentStop
```

```mdl
aspect useFollow
  desc: >
    The sticky tail as an intent — withdrawn only by a backwards scroll, never re-derived from
    proximity (corrections grow the document under a stationary reader). Optionally drives
    ScrollFollower for the velocity-based glide (rows/s, median row height) — DECIDED: wired and
    on by default, instant as the fallback (glide: false). Reusable for any streaming container:
    transcripts, logs.
  owns: following intent, tail correction, optional glide
```

```mdl
aspect useListSelection
  desc: >
    ADOPTED from react-ui-list, not rebuilt — single and multi modes exist there with ARIA
    semantics (aria-selected, dx-selected). Contribute a 'range' mode (shift-click, anchor+focus
    over the stops sequence). Selection is model-space ids, so it composes with virtualization
    untouched; the feed keeps its one SelectionGroup for cross-editor text selection.
  owns: selection value, mode policy (single | multi | range), row bindings
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Virtualizer invariants
  The properties every binding must hold; each is mutation-checked in placement.test.ts and the
  placement/* stories.
  req F-1.1: Prepending moves nothing at or after the anchor.
  req F-1.2: Measuring a row after the anchor never moves the anchor; measurements are keyed by id.
  req F-1.3: Corrections move the window's transform, never the scroll offset.
  req F-1.4: A scroll moves content by exactly what was scrolled — including upward from the tail,
    where unmeasured rows enter.
  req F-1.5: Reserve is a sizer term; the last row rests at the content's end, not the document's.
  req F-1.6: Edge drift is reported (onEdge), never silently applied.
  req F-1.7: Axis-neutral: block and inline are the same arithmetic; only the binding differs. In
    scope for the virtualizer including an inline acceptance story with real content; the feed list
    and rails stay vertical until a horizontal consumer exists.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Rendering
  req F-2.1: Block renderers are pluggable by kind — markdown (CodeMirror, cached shared extension
    sets), html, custom; room for json, transcript, tool-call blocks.
  req F-2.2: Chrome is a host render-prop and must not affect measurement beyond being inside the
    measured row.
  req F-2.3: Widgets (XML tag -> React via registry) may expand after mount; expansion is not a
    special case — it is the same post-commit measurement arriving again.
  req F-2.4: Widget state lives in a Root-owned store and survives its row unmounting.
  req F-2.5: The streaming item (FeedModel.streamingId) reconciles by delta rather than remounting.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Navigation
  req F-3.1: Stops are a model policy (FeedModel.stops via useStops); default is every message;
    isAnchor survives as fromMessages() sugar.
  req F-3.2: All drivers — toolbar, arrows, outliner, minimap — call useFeedNavigation; no parallel
    wiring.
  req F-3.3: The cursor is the row containing the scroll offset; every press travels.
  req F-3.4: Steps within the mounted window glide; far jumps are instant. Per-call behavior
    override, host default.
  req F-3.5: Cmd/Ctrl+Arrow jumps to first/last.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Selection
  req F-4.1: Selection modes single, multi, range are interchangeable policies (useListSelection).
  req F-4.2: Selection is model-space (ids) and survives virtualization; items read their own
    binding via useItemSelection(id), never a threaded selectedIds prop.
  req F-4.3: One SelectionGroup spans every editor for text selection.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Follow
  req F-5.1: Following is an intent; only a backwards scroll withdraws it, returning to the tail
    restores it.
  req F-5.2: An answer arriving while the reader is at the tail keeps the tail at rest on the
    viewport's end.
  req F-5.3: An answer arriving while the reader is elsewhere moves nothing.
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Rails
  req F-6.1: Outline ticks and card: pointer wins while pointing, keyboard while navigating,
    pointing again hands back; state observable via data-* attributes.
  req F-6.2: Minimap draws only from WindowState.geometry; viewport band stays inside the mounted
    band.
  req F-6.3: Both rails are 2rem wide by default; asserted equal.
  req F-6.4: Both rails live in react-ui-feed; Outline moves from react-ui-components with its
    call sites, leaving no re-export behind.
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Model
  req F-7.1: The virtualizer binds to ListModel; a prepend is told, never inferred by identity scan.
  req F-7.2: FeedModel is the native case: stops, streamingId, and iteration (loadBefore/loadAfter
    consumed by onEdge) are model concerns, not list props.
  req F-7.3: fromMessages(array) adapts the plain case; ECHO/queue bindings adapt outside this
    package.
  req F-7.4: Reactivity is @effect/atom; derivations (stops, decorations, readouts) are atoms over
    the model rather than parallel props.
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Retrofit
  req F-8.1: DONE — the virtualizer (placement + useWindow + Window + follow + ListModel + tests)
    lives in its own package, @dxos/react-ui-virtual; this package depends on it and the
    /virtualizer entry point is gone.
  req F-8.2: react-ui-mosaic VirtualStack (still on tanstack react-virtual) rebinds onto useWindow
    after the feed has soaked; its pagination hook becomes a ListModel.loadBefore/loadAfter
    consumer. Mosaic adds drag-and-drop, which the spike never exercised — behind a flag.
  req F-8.3: react-ui-list conventions adopted, not duplicated: useListSelection extended with
    range; listbox ARIA semantics for rows; useDecorations retrofitted to editor/table surfaces as
    they come up.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: Tail at rest with reserve
  given: 500 varied-height messages, a tail reserve on
  then:
    - the feed opens with the last message resting on the viewport's bottom edge
    - the reserve is still scrollable; the last row reaches the top of the viewport and no further
```

```mdl
test T-2: Upward scroll holds still
  given: the reader at the tail of a feed whose estimates are wrong for most rows
  when: scrolling upward in steps
  then: the row under the top of the viewport moves by exactly the scrolled distance
```

```mdl
test T-3: Prepend moves nothing
  given: a reader mid-feed
  when: a page of history is prepended
  then: no mounted row moves on screen
```

```mdl
test T-4: Follow
  given: a reader at the tail, streaming on
  when: an answer arrives
  then: the tail stays at rest; scrolling up during the stream stops the follow until the reader
    returns to the tail
```

```mdl
test T-5: One navigation seam
  given: a feed with per-prompt stops
  when: stepping via toolbar, arrows, outline, and minimap
  then: all four land on the same stops via the same controller, and the outline card follows
```

